{"content":"Found the bug: `Comparison.right` property returns `self.tokens[-2]` instead of `self.tokens[-1]`. Since Comparison groups like `x = NULL` have tokens `[Identifier, Whitespace, Comparison('='), Whitespace, <right-hand-side>]`, the last token is the actual right-hand value (NULL, 1.5, Parenthesis, etc.) and `tokens[-2]` is just the whitespace before it. This explains the `assert ' ' == 'NULL'` failure and the keywords/floats/parenthesis comparison test failures. Fixing it to use `tokens[-1]`.","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_1","name":"replace_text","arguments":{"path":"sqlparse/sql.py","old_text":"    @property
    def right(self):
        return self.tokens[-2]","new_text":"    @property
    def right(self):
        return self.tokens[-1]"}},{"id":"call_2","name":"run","arguments":{"command":"python -c "import sqlparse; s=sqlparse.parse('select * from foo where x = NULL')[0]; where = s.tokens[-1]; comp = where.tokens[-1]; print(repr(comp.left), repr(comp.right))""}},{"id":"call_3","name":"run","arguments":{"command":"python -c "import sqlparse; s=sqlparse.parse('select * from foo where x = 1.5')[0]; where = s.tokens[-1]; comp = where.tokens[-1]; print(repr(comp.left), repr(comp.right))""}},{"id":"call_4","name":"run","arguments":{"command":"python -c "import sqlparse; s=sqlparse.parse('select * from foo where x = (1)')[0]; where = s.tokens[-1]; comp = where.tokens[-1]; print(repr(comp.left), repr(comp.right))""}}]}

